      "id": "CUET_PHY_2026_P6_L6_Q01",
      "topic": "Electrostatics",
      "sub_topic": "Coulomb's Law",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "question": "Two point charges of +2 μC and +3 μC are placed 1 m apart in vacuum. What is the magnitude of the electrostatic force between them? (k = 9 × 10⁹ N m² C⁻²)",
      "options": [
        "A) 2.7 × 10⁻² N",
        "B) 5.4 × 10⁻² N",
        "C) 5.4 × 10⁻⁵ N",
        "D) 1.08 × 10⁻¹ N"
      ],
      "correct_option": "B",
      "explanation": "F = kq₁q₂/r² = 9×10⁹ × 2×10⁻⁶ × 3×10⁻⁶ / 1² = 54×10⁻³ = 5.4 × 10⁻² N."
    },
    {
